course: dictionary
lesson: 11865
title: Bookie and betting words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bookie is a person or company that takes bets. A bet is money you promise to hand over if something happens, like a horse winning a race. «The bookie paid out £20 to the man who picked the winning horse.» Paid out means handed money over, so the bookie is the one who pays the winners.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Dad went to the bookie's to place a bet on the football match.» The 's after bookie shows a place, so the bookie's is a betting shop. Bookie is an informal word, so you are more likely to hear it in chats and stories than in school books.
explain: «The bookies' favourite won the race, which surprised nobody.» Bookies' favourite means the horse the betting people thought was most likely to win. The words around it, won and surprised nobody, tell you the favourite was expected to win.
fact: A bookie is short for bookmaker, which is an informal word.
fact: «Bookie» means a person or company that takes bets and pays out money to winners.
fact: «The bookie's» means a betting shop.
fact: Gambling is risky, because most people who bet lose their money.
fact: «Favourite» in betting means the one most likely to win, and bookies' odds show how likely each one is.
exercise: «The bookie paid out £20 to the winner.» What does bookie mean? | A shop that sells books | A jockey who rides horses in races | *A person or company that takes bets and pays out money | A winner who gets money
exercise: «Dad went to the bookie's to place a bet.» What is the bookie's? | A bank for saving money | A library | *A betting shop | A football pitch
exercise: Why is gambling risky? | *Most people who bet lose their money | Bets never cost anything | Winning is always guaranteed | Bookies give away money for free
test: «The bookies' favourite was the grey horse.» What does favourite mean here? | *The horse most likely to win | The horse that always comes last | A horse that is too tired to run | A horse that is for sale
test: Bookie is short for which longer word? | Booklet | *Bookmaker | Bookshelf | Bookkeeper
exam: What does a bookie do? | Trains racing horses | *Takes bets and pays out winnings | Sells books in a shop | Referees football matches
